{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "about": "capri-syn's own measurements of the capri-desktop art (cell grid, anchors, loop/one-shot), taken from the PNGs at the pinned commits. Anchors and bounds are in cell px; x/y from the cell's top-left; bounds [x, y, w, h] = the union of every cell's opaque box. A laydown anchor's x is the figure's middle (edgeX: where her hanging leg leaves the surface). faces: the side her face looks to, unmirrored. fpsFrom 'clips.json' = lachy's quest clips.json lists the same frame count and cell width; 'guess' = ours. mirrorArt: the strip drawn for mirroring (same silhouette, the suit's asymmetric details swapped): when she faces the other way, draw mirror(mirrorArt), not mirror(strip). contact (seat and surface strips): on a window top, below cell row `line` only the columns `legs` [x0, x1) stay, the lower legs hanging over the edge; the window's front face hides the rest (a hand, the mane, an arm). glitchCells: cells with a chroma ghost drawn in (violet px > 2.5x the strip's median and > 1500 over it, measured on the pinned PNGs); a loop she holds skips them. capricore: CapriCore v1.2.2's own animations, drawn on her canvas (scale: canvas px per cell px; the cels are 512 px cells of the 1254 canvas). Its cel actions play cell by cell from moods.json (`<strip>#<cell>`, CapriCore's own timings: apps/desktop/renderer/hanging-cels.mjs); anchors are the v1.2.2 poses' (pose-ceiling's grip as the pack registers it, pose-sit-edge's seat) over the scale.",
